From b53270b38cb206738e5d1bcb056384a5b7a33d83 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Georgios Sokianos <walkero@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 13:12:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] c-strtod: avoid clash with AmigaOS exec/types.h's DOUBLE
 macro

AmigaOS SDK's <exec/types.h> defines DOUBLE to float64.  c-strtod.c's
own DOUBLE macro (expanding to double/long double) then redefines it,
which GCC flags as an error under -Werror:

lib/c-strtod.c:35: error: "DOUBLE" redefined [-Werror]

Undef it first so our local definition wins, matching how this file
already undefs its own macros before use.
---
 lib/c-strtod.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/lib/c-strtod.c b/lib/c-strtod.c
index 1511ab5640..a4a7931066 100644
--- a/lib/c-strtod.c
+++ b/lib/c-strtod.c
@@ -26,6 +26,10 @@
 #include <stdlib.h>
 #include <string.h>
 
+/* AmigaOS's <exec/types.h> already defines DOUBLE (to float64); undef
+   it first so it doesn't clash with the one defined here. */
+#undef DOUBLE
+
 #if LONG
 # define C_STRTOD c_strtold
 # define DOUBLE long double
-- 
2.53.0

